invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: ch_quic_switch_version takes a switch on a failed session, which
  then derives the keys of its one close under a version no packet of the
  connection carried. A session that fails at its ServerHello still waits
  for the ServerHello, holds no server byte after the wipe and has not
  switched, so its state is the one condition left to refuse it.
  test/quic_version_tests.h requires CH_EINVAL for a switch to version 2
  there.

--- old
    return q->endpoint == CH_QUIC_ENDPOINT_CLIENT && q->t.state == CH_ST_START &&
--- new
    return q->endpoint == CH_QUIC_ENDPOINT_CLIENT &&
